Mercury Windows SFX overlays
============================

This directory contains the three binary inputs that cannot be represented as
ordinary text patches:

- 7zSD.Win32.sfx: outer self-extractor used by x86 and x86-64 installers.
- 7zSD.ARM64.sfx: outer self-extractor used by ARM64 installers.
- setup.ico: Mercury icon embedded when the two executables are rebuilt.

Firefox deliberately checks prebuilt SFX executables into its source tree so
that packaging does not require Visual Studio. Mercury follows that model but
keeps all editable resource changes in
patches/firefox-153/170-mercury-windows-sfx-branding.patch. setup.sh copies
only these three files over the pinned Firefox tree; it does not replace the
7-Zip/LZMA SDK source or build projects.

Firefox stores resource.rc with CRLF line endings, so Git encodes patch 170 as
an exact binary delta. The decoded changes set CompanyName and LegalCopyright
to Alex313031, FileDescription to Mercury Browser Installer, ProductName to
Mercury, and the minimum-system message to Microsoft Windows 10 or newer.

