Rebuild procedure
-----------------

The preferred rebuild path is the manually dispatched
`.github/workflows/rebuild-windows-sfx.yml` workflow. It verifies both outputs,
and uploads them with SHA256SUMS.txt, BUILDINFO.json, and build provenance. The
workflow never modifies the repository. Download its artifact, inspect the
metadata, and manually replace both checked-in SFX files. Preserve BUILDINFO.json
with the release records and update the generated hash block above. The
workflow pins Windows SDK 10.0.22621.0 because the project's v142 ARM64
compiler is incompatible with the newer 10.0.26100.0 headers selected by an
unqualified `WindowsTargetPlatformVersion=10.0`. For a local rebuild:

1. Run setup.sh against FIREFOX_153_0_3_RELEASE so patch 170 and setup.ico are
   present in the Firefox checkout.
2. Follow other-licenses/7zstub/README.mozilla in that checkout.
3. Open other-licenses/7zstub/firefox/SFXSetup.sln with the Visual Studio 2022
   C++ x86 and ARM64 toolchains.
4. Build the ReleaseD configuration for x86 and ARM64.
5. Replace 7zSD.Win32.sfx and 7zSD.ARM64.sfx in this directory.
6. Verify both files' version resources, icon, architecture, minimum-Windows
   message, and SHA-256 hashes. Then build and launch each Windows installer.

Regenerate both executables whenever Firefox changes any file under
other-licenses/7zstub, even if Firefox does not update its checked-in binaries
in the same commit.
